            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.06545/2610.06545v1/toy.png",
                "caption": "Figure 3:Toy Experiment on Multimodal Sequence Structure.Each panel shows samples in the two-dimensional(x0,x1)(x_{0},x_{1})space, with the horizontal axis corresponding tox0x_{0}and the vertical axis corresponding tox1x_{1}.\nThebluepoints are sampled from the true data distribution while theorangepoints are generated by each model.\nAR tends to average over plausible modes and fails to recover the multimodal joint structure.\nGMM fails once the multimodal structure exceeds its finite mixture capacity.\nCausal VAE captures the major modes, but still produces noticeable inter-mode samples.\nIn contrast, EVA concentrates samples on the true modes and substantially suppresses inter-mode samples, indicating that the learned autoregressive prior better represents latent dependencies across sequence steps.\nBest viewed in zoom.",
                "position": 514
            }
        ]
